===== [6] verifier conclusions =====
(a) observed.txt shows the claimed defect: text Bitstring triple (40099, 0.5012375, 0.50579098043220405) and Literal triple (58, 0.0058, 0.0077560937775866317) both printed at -vv; JSON 'Most Common Value' carries mcvEstimateMode=58.0 PHat=0.0058 PU=0.007756093777586632 = the Literal triple; 3 mcvEstimate* keys; none of 40099 / 0.5012375 / 0.50579098043220405 occurs in the JSON text.
(b) control (1-bit fixture, same -i -vv -o, same N=10,000) runs one MCV estimate, 0 Bitstring lines, Literal mode 5008 == JSON 5008.0: no ambiguity. Differs in file+width (one logical change: binary vs non-binary data, which is what 3.1.3 keys the second estimate on). Supplementary -c probe on the SAME file: one Bitstring call, JSON triple == Bitstring (40099, 0.5012375, 0.505790980432204) -- confirms the README's unmeasured statement that the triple's meaning flips with the mode.
(c) PASS requires eq(json,literal) AND NOT eq(json,bitstring) AND NOT eq(literal,bitstring); absent text lines or <absent>/<no-case> JSON keys make float() raise, res is empty, and the script falls through to FAIL -- it cannot pass vacuously; tool rc checked. Mutation of the expectation (eq(j,l) -> eq(j,b)) produced NODEFECT / RESULT: FAIL exit 1; restored by cp, sha256 identical (1a8a1764...9b612); original re-run PASS exit 0.
Verdict: CONFIRMED. Severity LOW, direction neutral (hAssessed/hBitstring/hOriginal on the element are correct; only the intermediates triple is ambiguous). Already documented as F23 sub-claim (a) in audits/2026-09-30/AUDIT.md:53 and FINDINGS-TRACKER.md:1111 (status UNCONFIRMED); this reproducer confirms that sub-claim. Upstream-inherited: the overwrite is 64056aa (2022-02-21) and the disambiguating key was commented out in 04e8b4f (2022-02-16, 'not needed in every test case'); no fork repair touched tc631.
